invariant: INV-16
file: chacha20.c
catches: test/chacha-builds.sh
reason: chacha20.c's use_avx2 answers 1 whatever the session's ch_cfg.cpu says,
  so every session of an x86-64 host object runs the AVX2 kernel and dies
  of SIGILL on a CPU without AVX2. Every vector and equivalence case
  passes on a CPU with it, because the kernel computes the same bytes.
  The script compiles chacha20.c for x86-64 and requires chacha20_xor_cpu
  to call chacha20_vector_xor, the path a session without CH_CPU_AVX2
  runs.

--- old
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_AVX2) != 0;
--- new
    (void)cpu;
    return 1;
